  "title": "An intact Fano side never removes creation, and whether it adds any reduces to one pendant line",
  "subject": "Whether a side split from the Fano plane at a point acts as its line for creation",
  "conclusion": "Replacing a line by an intact Fano side never removes creation: the new knots off the side are those of the closed space, and generated knots through it have generated port shadows (proved through a tetrahedron form of the closure). That it never adds creation follows from the statement that one new point on one new line never does, which held on 117,344 cases but is not proved.",
